      "overview": "This lesson continues the study of the foundational terminology of ʿUlūm al-Ḥadīth (علوم الحديث), building upon previous discussions regarding the distinction between riwāyah (الرواية) and dirāyah (الدراية), and the definition of the science itself.\nThe preferred definition of ʿIlm al-Ḥadīth, as articulated by al-Ḥāfiẓ Ibn Ḥajar al-ʿAsqalānī (ابن حجر العسقلاني), is:\nمَعْرِفَةُ أَحْوَالِ الرَّاوِي وَالْمَرْوِيِّ\n“Knowledge of the conditions of the narrator and the narrated.”\nEarlier scholars such as Ibn Jamāʿah (ابن جماعة) expressed the definition in terms of sanad (السَّنَد) and matn (المَتْن), making it necessary to clarify these central terms. This lesson examines several key technical expressions used by the muḥaddithūn (المحدّثون), correcting misunderstandings and presenting their meanings systematically.",
