      "overview": "The science of ḥadīth (ʿulūmu al-ḥadīth) did not emerge in a fully systematized form from the earliest generations. Rather, its concepts, classifications, and terminology developed gradually as scholars sought to preserve, evaluate, and interpret the statements of the Prophet ﷺ. Among the most famous outcomes of this development is the threefold classification of ḥadīth into ṣaḥīḥ (صَحِيح), ḥasan (حَسَن), and ḍaʿīf (ضَعِيف).\nThis lesson examines the origins of this classification, the scholarly debates surrounding it, and the methodological principles that underlie how ḥadīth is categorized. It also highlights important corrections to common assumptions found in later summaries of the discipline.",
